nd set the fixture's expected commit-count target accordingly.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["COH","E2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'A single logical mutation that today emits the enrichment quartet + digest as separate commits emits ONE commit'","Step 2: 'Use that helper for the success finalize path so TICKET_DIGEST and DONE_ENRICH land in one commit'","Step 3: 'do not defer a visible claim past the LLM call ... keep the claim pre-LLM'"],"finding":"AC1 states the 'enrichment quartet + digest' collapses to ONE commit, but the implementation body only batches the success finalize pair (TICKET_DIGEST + DONE_ENRICH) and explicitly keeps the claim as a separate pre-LLM commit, so a single logical mutation still emits more than one commit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa8348c454de8a9e2","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1 vs Implementation plan steps 2-3","norm_id":"n78a119009d28f11d","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer reads AC1 as 'all of ENQUEUE/CLAIM/DONE_ENRICH/TICKET_DIGEST in one commit' but the body forbids batching the claim, leaving them unsure how many commits the fixture must observe."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Rewrite AC1 to name the batched set precisely, e.g. 'the finalize pair (TICKET_DIGEST + DONE_ENRICH) that today emits 2 commits now emits 1; the pre-LLM claim intentionally stays a separate commit for concurrency', and set the fixture assertion to that count.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Restate AC1/title so the batched unit is the finalize pair (TICKET_DIGEST + DONE_ENRICH) landing in ONE commit per drained item, and separately quantify that ENQUEUE (certification) and CLAIM (pre-LLM, intentionally un-batched) remain distinct commits — align the '4->1' framing in Context with the achievable '2 finalize writes -> 1 commit'.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Title: 'batch enrichment quartet + digest into one write lane'; AC1: 'emits ONE commit (one root-tree re-emission)'","queue.py:8 — 'ENQUEUE_ENRICH ... appended on plan-review CERTIFICATION' (a separate mutation, not the drain finalize)","_finalize_claims (enrich_drain.py:501-502) co-locates only ds.emit (TICKET_DIGEST) + _queue.mark_done (DONE_ENRICH); the CLAIM is appended in _collect_claims pre-LLM (enrich_drain.py:429) and step 3 explicitly refuses to defer/batch it","queue.claim reads back its own just-appended event to arbitrate the winner (queue.py:534-548), so batching the claim would break arbitration — the plan is right to keep it separate, which is precisely why 'ONE commit' for the whole quartet is unreachable"],"finding":"The mechanism can only batch the two finalize-phase events (TICKET_DIGEST + DONE_ENRICH); it cannot fold ENQUEUE (emitted at certification) or CLAIM (kept pre-LLM by design in step 3) into the same commit — so AC1's 'emits ONE commit' and the title's 'quartet + digest into one write lane' overstate the achievable reduction.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa457cc1186c9b9af","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1 / title / Implementation plan step 2-3","norm_id":"nb2ccfcd9175ebf96","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author writes the AC1 fixture expecting one commit and it observes ENQUEUE (from an earlier certification mutation) + CLAIM (collect) as distinct commits, so the count is >1 and the test either fails or is quietly weakened to only assert the DIGEST+DONE pair"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reframe: 'A drained item's finalize writes (TICKET_DIGEST + DONE_ENRICH) emit ONE commit instead of two.' Keep the note that CLAIM stays a separate pre-LLM commit for arbitration integrity, and adjust the per-mutation root-tree-emission count in AC5 accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the batch helper buffers DONE_ENRICH only when the TICKET_DIGEST event was successfully composed into the buffer, and that a compose-time failure of either event aborts the flush for that item so no partial finalize (DONE without DIGEST) is committed.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["digest_sidecar.emit and queue.mark_done wrap their append_event call in try/except and return False on failure (digest_sidecar.py:104-115, queue.py:82-95)","Under batch_sink, append_event only composes+buffers and returns without committing (_seam.py:636-639); the actual commit/failure surfaces at batch_write_and_push flush, OUTSIDE those functions' try/except","Step 4 requires 'DONE_ENRICH is not falsely recorded as a completed enrichment for a missing digest' — but if ds.emit's payload build raises (state read failure) it returns False today and mark_done still fires separately; the batched helper must not buffer DONE when the digest was not buffered"],"finding":"The plan does not specify how the batch helper reconciles the current per-call best-effort semantics of ds.emit/mark_done (each catches internally and returns bool) with deferred commit-time failure, where the commit no longer happens inside those functions but at flush.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3481136ed9d7d718","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan step 1/4 ('enrichment-local batch flush helper' / 'if digest emission fails ... DONE_ENRICH is not falsely recorded')","norm_id":"n85461db44373719a","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["ds.emit's content_hash/build_payload raises (unreadable state) so no TICKET_DIGEST is buffered, yet the helper still buffers+commits DONE_ENRICH — falsely tombstoning an enrichment with no digest, exactly the failure step 4 forbids"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a failure-injection test asserting the batched-commit rollback leaves no partial derived event staged/on disk and that a digest-emission failure does not falsely record DONE_ENRICH.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 4 states 'if a batched commit fails, the existing batch primitive rolls back the whole batch so no partial derived event is left staged/on disk' and 'if digest emission fails, enrichment remains best-effort and DONE_ENRICH is not falsely recorded'","The Test plan lists commit-count, observable-state, verify-authorship, and existing concurrency tests — none injects a digest-emission or batch-commit failure to assert no partial derived event / no false DONE_ENRICH"],"finding":"The plan specifies failure behavior (step 4: digest-emission failure stays best-effort with no false DONE_ENRICH; batched-commit failure rolls back the whole batch leaving nothing partial), but the Test plan / RED-first oracle enumerates no test that exercises either failure arm — the tests cover the happy batched write, observable-state equality, authorship, and existing concurrency, but not the rollback/best-effort disposition the plan newly relies on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f26ec17a073e9b61a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan (2026-08-31) > Test plan / RED-first oracle; step 4 of Mechanism","norm_id":"nc3a80fb9657ae6fb","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression that leaves a partial staged event or falsely records DONE_ENRICH on batch-commit failure would pass the current suite green, since no test injects the failure"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a test that forces the batch commit to fail (or the digest emit to raise) and asserts (a) neither TICKET_DIGEST nor DONE_ENRICH is persisted, and (b) no partial event file remains staged.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Cite ADR 0039 and justify batching the enrichment quartet+digest against its import-only carve-out (argue enrichment is import-like — opportunistic, idempotent-by-UUID, crash-resumable, advisory-locked, push-deferred — or update the ADR per its 'must revisit' clause).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ADR 0039 Decision 2: 'The batched path is import-only; interactive writes are never batched'","ADR 0039 Consequences: 'any future proposal to batch interactive writes must revisit this ADR'","Plan Mechanism reuses `_store.event_append.batch_write_and_push()` / `batch_stage_and_commit()` — the exact primitive ADR 0039 introduced and scoped","Enrichment queue/digest events append via `_seam.append_event` (queue.py:83, digest_sidecar.py:102), i.e. the store write path ADR 0039's durability invariant protects"],"finding":"The plan reuses the batched-commit primitive governed by ADR 0039 (batching scoped 'import-only'; 'any future proposal to batch interactive writes must revisit this ADR') without citing or reconciling that prior-art decision.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f827f1d6f841b01ad","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan (2026-08-31) > Mechanism","norm_id":"n5f9ae4ab15074c03","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or future maintainer checks W1's batching against ADR 0039's import-only scope and finds no engagement","Enrichment drain is treated as an 'interactive write' and the durability carve-out is silently violated without the ADR's required revisit"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a short subsection to Mechanism referencing docs/adr/0039-write-time-batched-commit-import-only.md, showing enrichment drain shares import's exemption rationale (already-deferred, idempotent/self-healing, not an interactive per-write durability guarantee) so batching trades commit granularity, not durability.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State, per altered failure arm, whether the disposition is retryable/transient (drain re-attempts next cycle) or fatal/permanent, especially for the batched-commit-failure arm.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'if digest emission fails, enrichment remains best-effort and DONE_ENRICH is not falsely recorded'","'if a batched commit fails, the existing batch primitive rolls back the whole batch' — states the rollback but not whether the drain retries or surfaces the failure as fatal for that item"],"finding":"The plan alters failure semantics on two arms (digest-emission failure and batched-commit failure) and states each arm's outcome inline ('best-effort', '